#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:3
#: 76d0419a6f784ed09765a93d93e83898
msgid "USB troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:7
#: c395341b3b98461c96cc485566959536
msgid "disp-sys-usb does not start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:10
#: 54daefb047c6479ca46d26031d00a72a
msgid ""
"If the disp-sys-usb does not start, it could be due to a PCI passthrough "
"problem. For more details on this issue along with possible solutions, look "
"at :ref:`PCI passthrough issues <user/troubleshooting/pci-troubleshooting:"
"pci passthrough issues>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:13
#: 0454e3aa7725482ca678a73250b72a27
msgid "Can't attach a USB device / USB device not showing in qvm-usb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:16
#: e88eadf6ae63411f9d4318d4d586f9bd
msgid ""
"To successfully attach a USB device, you require a VM dedicated to handling "
"the USB input and output. For guidance setting up a USB qube, see the :ref:"
"`USB documentation <user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-usb-devices:creating and "
"using a usb qube>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:18
#: 5050561291d1462988866db01caf503b
msgid ""
"Currently (until issue `1082 <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/"
"issues/1082>`__ gets implemented), if you remove the device before detaching "
"it from the qube, Qubes OS (more precisely, ``libvirtd``) will think that "
"the device is still attached to the qube and will not allow attaching "
"further devices under the same name. This may be characterized by VM manager "
"crashes and the error message: ``Houston, we have a problem``. The easiest "
"way to recover from such a situation is to reboot the qube to which the "
"device was attached. If this isn’t an option, you can manually recover from "
"the situation by following the instructions at the :ref:`Block Devices "
"documentation <user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-block-storage-devices:what if i "
"removed the device before detaching it from the vm?>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:21
#: 0715b24afc0d4700aca669812fcb25f2
msgid "\"Device attach failed\" error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:24
#: 53e53a47662d4d16935b17b2a40b80c9
msgid ""
"Upon trying to attach a USB device using the ``qvm-usb -a vm-name device-vm-"
"name:device`` command, you may face the error ``Device attach failed: no "
"device info received, connection failed, check backend side for details``. "
"This error mainly arises due to problems specific to the particular device, "
"such as the device being incompatible with qvm-usb or a broken cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:27
#: db1f0edf68d64c29a0407ce417f1ae32
msgid ""
"Attaching device to a qube works, but the device disconnects or disappears "
"upon usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:30
#: f5e97581709245799d61ed255e84a315
msgid ""
"After attaching a device to a qube, upon attempting to use the device "
"results in the device disappearing or disconnecting. This may be observed by "
"the device no longer existing in the Devices widget or the application "
"within the attached qube indicating the device is no longer found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:32
#: 1a3ad60c67d34e72bfc0c39ae1940a54
msgid ""
"As a first line of defense, increase the amount of memory given to the USB "
"VM (sys-usb). High-bandwidth devices such as webcams have been `observed "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues/6200>`__ to need more memory "
"in sys-usb. If increasing the amount of memory does not resolve the issue, "
"check kernel logs within sys-usb as well as the attached qube for errors "
"before filing a bug report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:35
#: 0b102b55e2be4931a31b41a7ded9d457
msgid "USB VM does not boot after creating and assigning USB controllers to it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:38
#: 874307eba7a74c2baec8afb7bb8781ce
msgid ""
"This is probably because one of the controllers does not support reset. In "
"Qubes R2 any such errors were ignored. In Qubes R3.x they are not. In R4.x, "
"devices that are automatically added to sys-net and sys-usb on install but "
"do not support FLR will be attached with the no-strict-reset option, but see "
"the related warning in the last sentence in this answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:40
#: 3bcb3c570c254885af43c321babe9766
msgid ""
"A device that does not support reset is not ideal and generally should not "
"be assigned to a VM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/usb-troubleshooting.rst:42
#: a08d3512c2e144bf8b35ed86de9933b4
msgid ""
"Most likely the offending controller is a USB 3.0 device. You can remove "
"this controller from the USB VM, and see if this allows the VM to boot. "
"Alternatively you may be able to disable USB 3.0 in the BIOS. If the BIOS "
"does not have the option to disable USB 3.0, try running the following "
"command in dom0 to force USB 2.0 modes for the USB ports:"
msgstr ""

